# Repo-root build context (infra/docker-compose.yml uses `context: ..` so
# apps/api and apps/web Dockerfiles can `pip install -e ../../services/*`).
# Without this file, every build sends the entire monorepo — including
# apps/api/.venv and apps/web/node_modules (~700MB combined) — to the Docker
# daemon on every invocation, which is what actually made api-worker's first
# build look hung rather than merely slow.
.git/
**/.venv/
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
apps/web/.next/
*.log
.DS_Store
